<http://data.silknow.org/object/cc57cded-b0f2-3541-b22f-78301fedae09>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Woven silk shawl, Lyon, France, ca. 1850."@en , "Shawl of woven silk, reversible with a double-cloth of black one side and red the other. The shawl has a deep floral border woven with additional bright blue, emerald, white, pink and dull yellow silk in sprays of exotic flowers.\nA nine-inch fringe is knotted into the shawl on all four edges is black on two and red on two. The pattern is woven in a warp-faced twill."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/8d1f6479-7622-387a-aa35-d90cce8f1465> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Woven silk shawl, Lyon, France, ca. 1850."@en , "Shawl of woven silk, reversible with a double-cloth of black one side and red the other. The shawl has a deep floral border woven with additional bright blue, emerald, white, pink and dull yellow silk in sprays of exotic flowers.\nA nine-inch fringe is knotted into the shawl on all four edges is black on two and red on two. The pattern is woven in a warp-faced twill."@en ;
